From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: L1519 fast draws, handle words checked on one translation of their span (EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS), off by default

Port of zortos293/Lichii PR #1519, commit 65745c2 (Zortos, "fast draws for computed texture
handles, handle words and dynamic vertex input", from #1161). Ported by reading, onto our
EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW (0559), which already carries most of it from #1161 itself.

Already in T181 with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1 + EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW=1 (not ported again): delta draws for
pipelines with computed texture handles (GraphicsPipeline::ComputedHandlesChanged under both cache
locks), handle data compared word by word, secondary words included, vertex attribute formats as
draw parameters with dynamic vertex input (IsL1161VertexFormat + the attribute type check), a full
range list widened instead of ending reuse (AppendConservativeRange, no uniform keeps then), and
verify counting only draws that held.

New here, with EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS=1 (exact "1", read once; needs EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1 and acts
only while EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW is on):
- TakeReusableDraw translates a handle buffer only over the bytes its handle words span
  (HandleRange), not the whole constant buffer, and compares the words on that one translation
  (Delta::ReachesWords: by device address when the span maps to one run of device memory, else
  any device write into the span counts). L1161 alone translated each word again, through one
  shared DeviceSpans, whenever a write reached the buffer.
- Words are sorted and merged per slot (MergedHandleWords) when the pipeline's word table is built.
- A write that reaches the span only between handle words keeps the delta draw but no uniform
  keeps (taken_delta.no_uniform_keeps), as upstream.
- With EDEN_NX2_NULL_POINTER_HANDLE on, texture words that are a storage buffer's address are left
  out of the merged words (ConfigureImpl binds no texture for them then). Upstream leaves them out
  always; ours reads them as handles without that switch, so they stay in.
- DeviceSpans records whether its range maps linearly (always computed in Update; read only here).

Not taken: FixedPipelineState::DynamicAttributeTypes (fixed_pipeline_state.* is a translation id
input; ours already has the function from an earlier patch), the pipeline cache's
g_dynamic_vertex_input (ours has g_vertex_formats_dynamic), the Reason::DeltaOverflow removal
(kept for the switch-off path), tests (src/tests not built here).

Line (Render_Vulkan, the first 16 checks a write reached, then powers of two):
"EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS: handle buffers checked over their words' span N, a write reached the
span N (not one device run N), reached a handle word N (full draw), only between the words N
(delta kept, no uniform keeps), merged words compared N, slots with no word left N".

Off: one bool per TakeReusableDraw that reaches the handle loop with L1161 on; DeviceSpans::Update
sets two fields more. Memory: per pipeline built with L1161 on, the merged word list and a
5x18 range table (about 0.7 KiB). Not in the kept-store stamp: nx2_fast_draw.*, vk_rasterizer.*,
vk_graphics_pipeline.* (KEEPS THE STORE).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.cpp b/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.cpp
index 5fdfd7cc95..be698c35ab 100644
--- a/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.cpp
@@ -18,7 +18,12 @@ void DeviceSpans::Update(const Tegra::MemoryManager& memory_, GPUVAddr address_,
     size = size_;
     map_serial = serial;
     spans.clear();
-    for (const auto& [device, bytes] : memory_.GetSubmappedDeviceRange(address_, size_)) {
+    const auto submapped = memory_.GetSubmappedDeviceRange(address_, size_);
+    // EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS (Lichii #1519): segments come in GPU order, joined where device
+    // memory continues; one segment of the whole size maps linearly. Only ReachesWords reads it.
+    linear = submapped.size() == 1 && submapped[0].second == size_;
+    linear_base = linear ? submapped[0].first : 0;
+    for (const auto& [device, bytes] : submapped) {
         spans.emplace_back(device, device + bytes);
     }
     std::ranges::sort(spans);
diff --git a/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h b/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h
index 6481f78db9..a8596061ec 100644
--- a/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h
+++ b/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h
@@ -122,6 +122,19 @@ inline constexpr std::array<const char*, static_cast<size_t>(Reason::Count)> rea
     return Common::LiveSwitch::Peek<Common::LiveSwitch::Id::L1161Draw>() != 0;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS=1 (exact "1") with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1, read once (zortos293/Lichii
+/// #1519, 65745c2, Zortos; from #1161): when EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW's handle check runs, a handle
+/// buffer is translated only over the bytes its handle words span (not the whole constant
+/// buffer), and the words are compared on that one translation (Delta::ReachesWords) instead of
+/// translating each word again. A write that reaches the buffer only between its handles keeps
+/// the delta draw but no uniforms. With EDEN_NX2_NULL_POINTER_HANDLE on, the words read as a
+/// storage buffer address (never a texture then) are left out of the words. Does nothing
+/// without EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW.
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool L1519FastDrawsEnabled() {
+    static const bool enabled = Enabled() && Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS");
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 /// EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP=1 with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1 (zortos293/Lichii #949: 6b38851501 and
 /// 3e86407514, zortos293): a delta draw binds a small streamed uniform buffer from the stream
 /// allocation the previous draw made for the same stage, slot, address and size in the same
@@ -207,11 +220,25 @@ public:
     /// Whether [begin, end) of device memory overlaps the range's.
     [[nodiscard]] bool Intersects(DAddr begin, DAddr end) const;
 
+    /// EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS (Lichii #1519): the GPU address the range starts at, and whether
+    /// it maps to one run of device memory in GPU order, starting at LinearBase.
+    [[nodiscard]] GPUVAddr Address() const noexcept {
+        return address;
+    }
+    [[nodiscard]] bool IsLinear() const noexcept {
+        return linear;
+    }
+    [[nodiscard]] DAddr LinearBase() const noexcept {
+        return linear_base;
+    }
+
 private:
     const Tegra::MemoryManager* memory{};
     GPUVAddr address{};
     u64 size{};
     u64 map_serial{};
+    bool linear{};
+    DAddr linear_base{};
     std::vector<std::pair<DAddr, DAddr>> spans; ///< Sorted, disjoint [begin, end) pairs
 };
 
@@ -264,6 +291,39 @@ struct Delta {
         }
         return false;
     }
+
+    /// EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS (zortos293/Lichii #1519, 65745c2): Reaches for only the bytes
+    /// [base + first, base + second) of each of `words` (sorted byte offsets of one constant
+    /// buffer at `base`), all inside the range `spans` was updated with. Device writes are
+    /// compared word by word when that range maps linearly, else with the whole range (true when
+    /// one reaches it anywhere: conservative).
+    template <typename Words>
+    [[nodiscard]] bool ReachesWords(GPUVAddr base, const Words& words,
+                                    const DeviceSpans& spans) const {
+        for (u32 write = 0; write < num_writes; ++write) {
+            for (const auto& [first, second] : words) {
+                if (write_begin[write] < base + second && base + first < write_end[write]) {
+                    return true;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        for (u32 write = 0; write < num_device_writes; ++write) {
+            if (!spans.Intersects(device_begin[write], device_end[write])) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            if (!spans.IsLinear()) {
+                return true;
+            }
+            for (const auto& [first, second] : words) {
+                const DAddr begin = spans.LinearBase() + (base + first - spans.Address());
+                const DAddr end = begin + (second - first);
+                if (device_begin[write] < end && begin < device_end[write]) {
+                    return true;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        return false;
+    }
 };
 
 inline Delta g_delta;
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp
index 7643e5f3bc..a876f4fb14 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_graphics_pipeline.cpp
@@ -1113,27 +1113,59 @@ bool GraphicsPipeline::ConfigureImpl(bool is_indexed) {
 
 void GraphicsPipeline::BuildHandleWords() {
     handle_words = std::make_unique<HandleWordTable>();
+    // EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS (Lichii #1519): a texture element whose word is a storage buffer
+    // address binds no texture with EDEN_NX2_NULL_POINTER_HANDLE (ConfigureImpl), so a write to
+    // it changes nothing a full resolve gives. Left out of `merged` only, and only then.
+    const bool null_pointer_handles = VideoCommon::NullPointerHandlesEnabled();
     {
         for (size_t stage = 0; stage < NUM_STAGES; ++stage) {
+            const auto& info = stage_infos[stage];
             const auto add = [&](const auto& desc) {
                 if (desc.handle_program != ~0U) return;
-                const auto range = [&](u32 slot, u32 offset) {
+                const auto range = [&](u32 slot, u32 offset, bool primary) {
                     precise_handle_buffers[stage] |= 1U << slot;
                     for (u32 i = 0; i < desc.count; ++i) {
                         const u32 first = offset + (i << desc.size_shift);
                         handle_words->words[stage][slot].emplace_back(first, first + 4);
+                        if constexpr (std::is_same_v<std::remove_cvref_t<decltype(desc)>,
+                                                     Shader::TextureDescriptor>) {
+                            if (primary && null_pointer_handles &&
+                                VideoCommon::HandleIsStoragePointer(info, desc, i)) {
+                                continue;
+                            }
+                        }
+                        handle_words->merged[stage][slot].emplace_back(first, first + 4);
                     }
                 };
-                range(desc.cbuf_index, desc.cbuf_offset);
+                range(desc.cbuf_index, desc.cbuf_offset, true);
                 if constexpr (requires { desc.has_secondary; }) {
-                    if (desc.has_secondary) range(desc.secondary_cbuf_index, desc.secondary_cbuf_offset);
+                    if (desc.has_secondary) {
+                        range(desc.secondary_cbuf_index, desc.secondary_cbuf_offset, false);
+                    }
                 }
             };
-            const auto& info = stage_infos[stage];
             for (const auto& desc : info.texture_buffer_descriptors) add(desc);
             for (const auto& desc : info.image_buffer_descriptors) add(desc);
             for (const auto& desc : info.texture_descriptors) add(desc);
             for (const auto& desc : info.image_descriptors) add(desc);
+            // EDEN_UP_L1519_FAST_DRAWS: sorted, overlapping or touching words joined, and the
+            // span they cover (upstream's handle_words / handle_ranges).
+            for (u32 slot = 0; slot < Maxwell::MaxConstBuffers; ++slot) {
+                auto& list = handle_words->merged[stage][slot];
+                std::ranges::sort(list);
+                size_t joined = 0;
+                for (const auto& word : list) {
+                    if (joined != 0 && word.first <= list[joined - 1].second) {
+                        list[joined - 1].second = (std::max)(list[joined - 1].second, word.second);
+                    } else {
+                        list[joined++] = word;
+                    }
+                }
+                list.resize(joined);
+                if (!list.empty()) {
+                    handle_words->ranges[stage][slot] = {list.front().first, list.back().second};
+                }
+            }
         }
     }
 
